job_description:
No grupo Bluehost (grupo do qual a Hostgator faz parte), acreditamos que todas as pequenas empresas merecem a oportunidade de prosperar online. Nossa missão é dar às pequenas empresas a confiança necessária para pensar grande. Somos a plataforma completa para que as pequenas empresas cresçam online com simplicidade poderosa, desempenho premium, ferramentas inteligentes e suporte humano. 


E aí, bora fazer parte disso tudo? **#VemSerGator** **#Hostgator**✨ 

Estamos buscando um Product Manager com **perfil técnico e de negócios** bem desenvolvido para nossa empresa!



**O que você fará:**  

* Descobrir oportunidades e entregar soluções em colaboração com as equipes de Design, Engenharia e Negócios;
* Entender a fundo os diferentes perfis de clientes, analisando dados e comportamentos para aprimorar nossos produtos;
* Definir e priorizar o roadmap de produtos junto ao time, garantindo alinhamento estratégico;
* Elaborar user stories e participar do desenvolvimento do produto, garantindo clareza no backlog e nos critérios de aceite;
* Conduzir pesquisas de mercado e concorrência, contribuindo com insights estratégicos;
* Acompanhar e analisar métricas de desempenho, garantindo que os resultados esperados sejam atingidos;
* Conduzir workshops e sessões de ideação, como elaboração de jornadas do cliente e prototipação de soluções.



**Quem você é:**  

* Experiência sólida atuando com Produtos digitais - segmento de Hosting é um diferencial;
* Foco em resultados: você mede e otimiza o impacto de suas iniciativas;
* Excelentes habilidades de comunicação e colaboração com diversas áreas, especialmente com equipes de Design e Engenharia;
* Conhecimento em desenvolvimento ágil e mindset voltado para evolução contínua;
* Capacidade analítica: experiência com levantamento e análise de dados quantitativos e qualitativos para tomada de decisão.
* Inglês avançado.



**Porque você vai nos amar**  

* Por aqui somos #HostGatorEverywhere: Vaga 100% remota, com ajuda de custo mensal pro home office de R$180,00 e uma ajuda de custo extra para adquirir itens pro seu escritório
* Oferecemos Vale-Refeição ou Vale-Alimentação no valor de R$44,55 por dia trabalhado
* Plano de saúde e odontológico, sem coparticipação para o colaborador
* Programa de bem-estar: Gympass, meditação online e telemedicina!
* Você tem um cachorro, gato, coelho, hamster, cabra, tartaruga ou até mesmo um mini dragão? Temos parceria com plano de saúde pet!
* Plataforma educacional: você poderá fazer graduação, pós-graduação, cursos de idiomas (e muito mais!) em mais de 100 instituições de ensino por um valor super acessível!
* Seguro de vida
* Hospedagem de sites gratuita



E muuuuuuito mais!  



*Todas as nossas vagas estão disponíveis para pessoas com deficiência (PCD).*

# Warehouse Operative – Direct to Consumer

Stoke on Trent, Staffordshire

Full Time

Share job

At our national distribution centre, we stock over 16,000 (29,000 including specials) veterinary products including pharmaceuticals, instruments, pet products and accessories.  The Warehouse Operative role is at the heart of what we at NVS do.  The role involves picking and preparing customer orders ready for next day despatch, in compliance with SOPs.

Apply Now

**Key Responsibilities**

On our warehouse noon and night shifts there are various activities, including: picking, checking and replenishment. General tasks include:

* Picking a broad range of veterinary products including controlled drugs, items which must be kept between 2 and 8 degrees, bulk items, hazardous and cytotoxic products and other specialist items, using a paper-based pick note;
* Some work at height (accessed via ladders/kick-steps), and below the knee;
* Replenishing stock where necessary;
* Checking orders and inputting batching information onto the computer system to allow despatched stock trackability;
* Ensuring items are packed is such a way as to limit the risk of damages to products;
* Compliance with Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs);
* Moving orders ready for despatch;
* Loading vehicles.

**General**

* Required to take a flexible approach, supporting other teams as necessary;
* Maintain good distribution practices, including a ‘clean as you go approach’;
* Focused on H&S;
* Basic IT work;
* Regular manual handling of products, up to 16kg (up to 25kg in Bulk area);
* Operating LLOP, pump trucks, electric pump truck and HLOP;
* A busy and physically demanding role;
* A diverse and inclusive culture;
* Required to work in fridges as necessary.
* Operatives are required to perform any other reasonable duties as the business requires.

**Personal attributes:** Qualifications, experience, skills, knowledge and competencies required to fulfil the role

* Some experience of working in a warehouse environment would be advantageous but is not essential;
* GCSE grades D-G or equivalent is desirable;
* A good level of attention to detail;
* The ability to work accurately under pressure;
* Good literacy and numeracy skills;
* The ability to work with others;
* Effective communication;
* Act in a professional manner;
* Hard-working, self-motivated and customer focused;
* Looks for opportunities to improve processes and channels suggestions appropriately.

*Applicants should be aware that in line with our Drugs and Alcohol policy we reserve the right to conduct* *random drug and alcohol* *tests.*

*NVS Group is committed to equality of opportunity and this underpins our employment and recruitment procedures. We use objective, job-related criteria when making appointment decisions and our selection criteria is based on skills, experience, qualifications, and an ability to do the job.*

Due to the large number of applications, we receive, we regret that we will not contact candidates that have not been selected for interview. If you have not heard from us within 2 weeks, you should assume that you have not been successful on this occasion.

*By continuing with your application for employment you are confirming you agree with our Privacy Notice*

# Warehouse Operative – Goods In

Stoke on Trent, Staffordshire

Full Time

Share job

At our national distribution centre, we stock over 16,000 (29,000 including specials) veterinary products including pharmaceuticals, instruments, pet products and accessories.  The Warehouse Operative role is at the heart of what we at NVS do.  The role involves unloading, unpacking and replenishing goods, in compliance with SOPs.

Apply Now

**Key Responsibilities**

On our warehouse day shift there are various activities, including: unloading HGVs, breaking deliveries down, picking and replenishment of stock. Dealing with a broad range of veterinary products including controlled drugs, items which must be kept between 2 and 8 degrees, bulk items, hazardous and cytotoxic products and other specialist items.  General tasks include:

* Unloading incoming stock from HGVs and LCV;
* Breaking down stock into relevant unit of measure and area using a paper-based system;
* Unloading HGVs returning from our Depots of totes, pallets, ranger cages, fridges, waste/recycling and returned stock;
* Replenishing stock;
* Stock put away;
* Picking Bulk orders;
* Inputting information onto the computer system to allow stock trackability;
* Compliance with Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs);
* Some work at height (accessed via ladders/kick-steps), and below the knee;

**General**

* Required to take a flexible approach, supporting other teams as necessary;
* Maintain good distribution practices, including a ‘clean as you go approach’;
* Focused on H&S;
* Basic IT work;
* Regular manual handling of products, up to 16kg (up to 25kg in Bulk area);
* Operating LLOP, pump trucks, electric pump truck, HLOP, reach truck, counter balance and VNA;
* A busy and physically demanding role;
* A diverse and inclusive culture.
* Requirement to work in fridge area on a rota basis.

Operatives are required to perform any other reasonable duties as the business requires.

**Personal attributes:** Qualifications, experience, skills, knowledge and competencies required to fulfil the role

* Some experience of working in a warehouse environment would be advantageous but is not essential;
* GCSE grades D-G or equivalent is desirable;
* A good level of attention to detail;
