## Job description

No Grupo Stefanini, acreditamos no poder da colaboração. Co-criamos soluções inovadoras em parceria com nossos clientes, combinando tecnologia de ponta, inteligência artificial e a criatividade humana. Estamos na vanguarda da resolução de problemas de negócios, proporcionando impacto real em escala global.

Ao se juntar à Stefanini, você se torna parte de uma jornada global de transformação. Estamos empenhados em criar impacto positivo não apenas nos negócios, mas também na vida de nossos colaboradores. Se você procura uma oportunidade de crescimento profissional em uma empresa que valoriza inovação, respeito, autonomia e parceria, você encontra aqui!

Junte-se a nós e seja parte da mudança!

#LI-MB1

#LI-REMOTE

## Responsibilities and assignments

Procuramos um(a) desenvolvedor(a) experiente para atuar na manutenção e modernização de sistemas corporativos, em um projeto temporário com duração de aproximadamente 3 meses, com possibilidade de extensão. O profissional trabalhará com tecnologias legadas e modernas, atuando na manutenção de sistemas desenvolvidos em Delphi 7 que implementam regras de negócio complexas, além de contribuir em aplicações recentes desenvolvidas em Python/Django. Essa posição exige habilidade em diagnosticar e solucionar problemas, garantir a estabilidade dos sistemas e oferecer suporte durante a migração de ambientes.

**Responsabilidades:**

* Analisar e manter sistemas legados desenvolvidos em Delphi 7, assegurando a integridade e a consistência das regras de negócio;
* Atuar no desenvolvimento e aprimoramento de aplicações em Python/Django, especialmente nas interfaces e funcionalidades recentes;
* Apoiar a migração do banco de dados Oracle 9 para Oracle 19, contribuindo para a atualização, padronização e melhorias de performance;
* Realizar testes e identificar problemas de compatibilidade, garantindo a continuidade dos serviços durante o processo de transição;
* Colaborar com a equipe para propor soluções e otimizações, mantendo a estabilidade e eficiência dos sistemas críticos.

## Requirements and qualifications

* Experiência sólida com Delphi 7 e manutenção de sistemas legados;
* Conhecimentos em Python e Django, com habilidade para implementar e atualizar funcionalidades;
* Vivência com Oracle, especialmente em processos de migração ou atualização de versões de banco de dados;
* Capacidade analítica para compreender e solucionar problemas envolvendo regras de negócio complexas;
* Proatividade, foco em resultados e habilidade para trabalhar de forma autônoma em ambientes críticos.

## Additional information

🍛 Vale-alimentação ou vale-refeição;

👨🏼‍🎓 Desconto em cursos, universidades e instituições de idiomas;

📚 Academia Stefanini — plataforma com cursos on-line, gratuitos, atualizados e com certificado;

🗣 Mentoring;

💉 Clube de vantagens para consultas e exames;

🏥 Assistência médica;

🦷 Assistência odontológica;

💰 Clube de vantagens e descontos nos melhores estabelecimentos;

🛫 Clube de viagens;

🐶 Convênio para pets.

## Employee Relations Case Manager

Apply

:   London

:   Full time

:   Posted 4 Days Ago

:   R5918

The TP ICAP Group is a world leading provider of market infrastructure.

Our purpose is to provide clients with access to global financial and commodities markets, improving price discovery, liquidity, and distribution of data, through responsible and innovative solutions.

Through our people and technology, we connect clients to superior liquidity and data solutions.

The Group is home to a stable of premium brands. Collectively, TP ICAP is the largest interdealer broker in the world by revenue, the number one Energy & Commodities broker in the world, the world’s leading provider of OTC data, and an award winning all-to-all trading platform.

The Group operates from more than 60 offices in 27 countries.  We are 5,300 people strong.  We work as one to achieve our vision of being the world’s most trusted, innovative, liquidity and data solutions specialist.

**Role Overview**

The role sits within HR and partners with HR and business managers in the delivery of a proactive employee relations offering.  This is an individual who can quickly build relationships as a  trusted advisor through their ability to effectively and pragmatically communicate, delivering consistent and clear advice on Employee Relations (“ER”) issues.  Working as part of a team is key to being successful in this role.

**Role Responsibilities**

The purpose of the role is to minimise risk of employee issues through:



* Management of the internal processes for disciplinary matters and formal complaints; preparing and reviewing case related documentation; working with independent hearing officers; drafting outcome letters and reporting/following up on any recommendations and conclusions;
* Providing guidance and direction to HR Advisory partners on end to end employee relations matters including but not limited to: performance, capability, conduct, redundancies, settlement agreements, exit discussions and sickness absence process. This includes reviewing and drafting documentation;
* Ensuring consistency of process and outcomes when managing employee related risk through the documentation and review of toolkits and guidance;
* The development and delivery of training for independent hearing officers, HR Advisory, managers and employees;
* Providing problem resolution/support to HR Business Partners, HR leadership team and business leaders for all complex ER matters;
* Ensuring that the relationship between TP ICAP and its employees is managed appropriately, identifying key risks to the business and to the HR leadership team;
* Supporting policy development in line with best practice, legal requirements and in support of strategic objectives;
* Convening and facilitating internal Committee meetings;
* The promotion of a progressive culture through the management of ER cases;
* Effectively managing relationships with key internal stakeholders working closely with and also ensuring that functional boundaries are acknowledged and adhered, particularly with Compliance and Legal functions;
* Providing the HR global leadership team with regular updates and overseeing the production of statistical reporting;
* Collaboration with control partners on all aspects of conduct management;
* Receiving and reviewing management information (MI) relating to breaches and trends; and considering this information when reviewing conduct;

**Experience / Competences**

Essential

* Demonstrable experience with ER case management within a front office, Financial Service environment
* Sound understanding of employment law and the practical application in managing employee related risk
* Significant hands-on experience of dealing with ER matters such as conduct and complaints, employee sickness/health & wellbeing, performance management, employment disputes, including within a front office Financial Services environment
* Experience in dealing with business restructuring such as head count reduction, TUPE, office moves, etc.
* Wants to work as a team player and enjoys discussing and advising on employee related topics
* Collaborates with stakeholders within and outside of the immediate department ‘to get the job done’



Desired

* Legal background

**Role Band & Level:** Manager, 7



